{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41847","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74665","text":"Round 27, pass B4 — the pool closes, and your three rulings taken"}]},{"id":"blk-41848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74666","marks":["bold"],"text":"All three B3 rulings implemented, and steps 1–7 of your ordering done in one round as you asked. Every rule of the declared pool now has a positive native witness."},{"id":"spn-74667","text":" Steps 8 (BUDGET_EXHAUSTED as film evidence) and 9 ("},{"id":"spn-74668","marks":["code"],"text":"EMISSION_CONFORMANCE-v1"},{"id":"spn-74669","text":") are the next two rounds, untouched."}]},{"id":"blk-41849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74670","text":"Gate: grid "},{"id":"spn-74671","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.42.0"},{"id":"spn-74672","text":" (89 entries / 379 citations) · "},{"id":"spn-74673","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-74674","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74675","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.4.0"},{"id":"spn-74676","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-74677","marks":["bold"],"text":"298/298"},{"id":"spn-74678","text":" · film "},{"id":"spn-74679","marks":["bold"],"text":"32/32"},{"id":"spn-74680","text":" · lowering 23/23 · bridge 48/48 · derive 45/45 · realm 24/24 · "},{"id":"spn-74681","marks":["bold"],"text":"measure-compare 35/35 (non-gating)"},{"id":"spn-74682","text":". "},{"id":"spn-74683","marks":["code"],"text":"cert_id a08ee15d…"},{"id":"spn-74684","text":" byte-identical — "},{"id":"spn-74685","marks":["bold"],"text":"thirty-seventh"},{"id":"spn-74686","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41850","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74687","text":"(a) The family ID — taken exactly"}]},{"id":"blk-41851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74688","marks":["code"],"text":"impl-c-ic32-film-v0.1.0"},{"id":"spn-74689","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-74690","marks":["bold"],"text":"`impl-c-ic32-film`"},{"id":"spn-74691","text":". No "},{"id":"spn-74692","marks":["code"],"text":"-gen1"},{"id":"spn-74693","text":": nothing about the lineage has changed, so a generation marker would be inventing a distinction to fill a space the old name left. No compensating "},{"id":"spn-74694","marks":["code"],"text":"implementation_version"},{"id":"spn-74695","text":" field either — the digest is the provenance, and the binary's human-readable version stays descriptive."}]},{"id":"blk-41852","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74696","marks":["code"],"text":"probe_execlaunch_v09_repro.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74697","text":" keeps the old string. It is a dated record of what the catalog said in its era; rewriting a frozen witness to agree with the present falsifies the witness."}]},{"id":"blk-41853","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74698","text":"(b) The one-interaction guard — kept, and its prediction now measured"}]},{"id":"blk-41854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74699","text":"Guard unchanged and post-hoc, for your reason: it sees what the runtime "},{"id":"spn-74700","marks":["italic"],"text":"did"},{"id":"spn-74701","text":", including any future change inside "},{"id":"spn-74702","marks":["code"],"text":"fire()"},{"id":"spn-74703","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-74704","marks":["code"],"text":"whnf()"},{"id":"spn-74705","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41855","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74706","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32_film --probe-whnf"},{"id":"spn-74707","text":" measures the prediction. It asks the "},{"id":"spn-74708","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-74709","text":" classifier what heads it admits and reports per class — no second inline recognizer, because two semantic recognizers drift:"}]},{"id":"blk-41856","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"DUP-LAM   delta=0  state=same        DUP-ERA   delta=0  state=same\nDUP-SUP=  delta=0  state=same        DUP-VAR   delta=0  state=same\nDUP-SUP!  delta=0  state=same        DUP-APP   delta=0  state=same"},{"id":"blk-41857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74710","text":"Your semantic-state clause is the one that earns its keep: "},{"id":"spn-74711","marks":["code"],"text":"whnf"},{"id":"spn-74712","text":" memoizes a stuck application's reduced head into its slot "},{"id":"spn-74713","marks":["bold"],"text":"without counting an interaction"},{"id":"spn-74714","text":", so a counter alone would have called that inert for the wrong reason."}]},{"id":"blk-41858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74715","marks":["bold"],"text":"Your fail-stop caveat is recorded in three places"},{"id":"spn-74716","text":" — the C header, the law statement, and the witness's own output line — rather than left for a future session to rediscover."}]},{"id":"blk-41859","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74717","text":"(c) The "},{"id":"spn-74718","marks":["code"],"text":"t:"},{"id":"spn-74719","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-74720","marks":["code"],"text":"v:"},{"id":"spn-74721","text":" alias — you were right that it is not a non-question"}]},{"id":"blk-41860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74722","text":"Your framing is now the law text: the locus is committed into "},{"id":"spn-74723","marks":["code"],"text":"frame_id"},{"id":"spn-74724","text":", so two spellings of one transition would be "},{"id":"spn-74725","marks":["bold"],"text":"two canonical frame identities for the same pre, rule and post"},{"id":"spn-74726","text":", and D-7's uniqueness result would gain an exception."}]},{"id":"blk-41861","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74727","text":"The emitter checks injectivity at "},{"id":"spn-74728","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-74729","text":" enabled state and refuses "},{"id":"spn-74730","marks":["code"],"text":"film-locus-alias"},{"id":"spn-74731","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-41862","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74732","marks":["code"],"text":"I-1"},{"id":"spn-74733","text":" computes the same property on the kernel's node graph: **44 distinct enabled redexes across 21"}]}],"id":"blk-41864","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74734","text":"states of "},{"id":"spn-74735","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-74736","text":", 0 with more than one canonical locus.** Reported at zero, because a diagnostic that only speaks when it fires is indistinguishable from one never wired in."}]},{"id":"blk-41867","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74737","text":"Per-runtime, not cross-implementation — physical identity isn't comparable, exactly as you said."}]}],"id":"blk-41868","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74738","marks":["bold"],"text":"Precedence stays unruled and the emitter refuses rather than picks."},{"id":"spn-74739","text":" If a well-formed fixture ever"}]}],"id":"blk-41870","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74740","text":"produces one, the answer is your earliest-occurrence rule, not blessing both."}]},{"id":"blk-41873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74741","text":"Independently of your scan: 0 alias hits across all 35 measured fixtures on the JS side too."}]},{"id":"blk-41874","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74742","text":"The ERA witnesses — by construction"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-41876","spans":[{"id":"spn-74743","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-41877","spans":[{"id":"spn-74744","text":"fixture"}]},{"id":"blk-41878","spans":[{"id":"spn-74745","text":"film"}]}],"id":"blk-41875","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-41879","spans":[{"id":"spn-74746","text":"E-1"}]},{"id":"blk-41880","spans":[{"id":"spn-74747","marks":["code"],"text":"(* x)"}]},{"id":"blk-41881","spans":[{"id":"spn-74748","text":"one "},{"id":"spn-74749","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74750","text":" frame at "},{"id":"spn-74751","marks":["code"],"text":"t:"},{"id":"spn-74752","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-74753","marks":["code"],"text":"*"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41882","spans":[{"id":"spn-74754","text":"E-2"}]},{"id":"blk-41883","spans":[{"id":"spn-74755","marks":["code"],"text":"!{a,b} = *; λz.a"}]},{"id":"blk-41884","spans":[{"id":"spn-74756","text":"one "},{"id":"spn-74757","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74758","text":" frame at "},{"id":"spn-74759","marks":["code"],"text":"d:0"},{"id":"spn-74760","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-74761","marks":["code"],"text":"λa.*"}]}],[{"id":"blk-41885","spans":[{"id":"spn-74762","text":"E-3"}]},{"id":"blk-41886","spans":[{"id":"spn-74763","marks":["code"],"text":"!{a,b} = *; (a b)"}]},{"id":"blk-41887","spans":[{"id":"spn-74764","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74765","text":" then "},{"id":"spn-74766","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74767","text":", both projections live"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-41888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74768","text":"Measured on the kernel first, then built. "},{"id":"spn-74769","marks":["bold"],"text":"E-2 earns its place twice"},{"id":"spn-74770","text":": only the left projection is reachable, so it takes the "},{"id":"spn-74771","marks":["bold"],"text":"one-sided path through `find_projections`"},{"id":"spn-74772","text":" that no two-projection fixture exercises; E-3 is the other side, where the sibling resolves through the substitution ic32 writes into "},{"id":"spn-74773","marks":["code"],"text":"heap[D]"},{"id":"spn-74774","text":". All three replay on "},{"id":"spn-74775","marks":["code"],"text":"FloatRt"},{"id":"spn-74776","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-74777","marks":["code"],"text":"DescFloatRt"},{"id":"spn-74778","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74779","text":"Forgeries: "},{"id":"spn-74780","marks":["bold"],"text":"E-4"},{"id":"spn-74781","text":" "},{"id":"spn-74782","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-ERA"},{"id":"spn-74783","text":"→"},{"id":"spn-74784","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-LAM"},{"id":"spn-74785","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-74786","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-rule-mismatch"},{"id":"spn-74787","text":", unforgeable before this round because APP-ERA had never been emitted) and "},{"id":"spn-74788","marks":["bold"],"text":"E-5"},{"id":"spn-74789","text":" the dup-over-eraser at "},{"id":"spn-74790","marks":["code"],"text":"d:7"},{"id":"spn-74791","text":" on a fixture with exactly one live cell ("},{"id":"spn-74792","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-locus-not-enabled"},{"id":"spn-74793","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-41890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74794","marks":["bold"],"text":"The corpus could never have found these."},{"id":"spn-74795","text":" The 24 vectors contain "},{"id":"spn-74796","marks":["bold"],"text":"no ERA at all"},{"id":"spn-74797","text":" — which is how all 24 could agree while two of nine rules had never run natively."}]},{"id":"blk-41891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74798","marks":["bold"],"text":"One thing I measured rather than argued:"},{"id":"spn-74799","text":" ic32's APP-ERA runs "},{"id":"spn-74800","marks":["code"],"text":"collect()"},{"id":"spn-74801","text":", freeing the discarded argument's built spine. Under free scheduling rather than demand-driven "},{"id":"spn-74802","marks":["code"],"text":"whnf"},{"id":"spn-74803","text":", \"uniquely owned\" is an assumption, and a wrongly freed slot would be reallocated and surface as a post-state divergence. Kept (the runtime under test must be the runtime that ships); the C↔JS agreement on the ERA fixtures is what says it is safe here."}]},{"id":"blk-41892","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74804","text":"Two ratchets, and one weakening the battery caught in a single run"}]},{"id":"blk-41893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74805","marks":["bold"],"text":"The scope predicate stopped naming a rule, on its fourth move."},{"id":"spn-74806","text":" dup PRESENCE → dup ENABLEDNESS → the two ERA rules → nothing rule-shaped. Twice the grid assertion pinning it blocked the round that closed the gap. It now pins the durable property all four spellings were instances of: "},{"id":"spn-74807","marks":["italic"],"text":"an enumerated rule the emitter cannot fire refuses BY NAME rather than being silently skipped."}]},{"id":"blk-41894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74808","marks":["bold"],"text":"Same disease one level up:"},{"id":"spn-74809","text":" the "},{"id":"spn-74810","marks":["code"],"text":"@1"},{"id":"spn-74811","text":"-is-history assertion had to be edited each time the law superseded. Generalised to the shape — exactly one canonical revision, it must be the latest, every superseded one on the record saying so."}]},{"id":"blk-41895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74812","marks":["bold"],"text":"And my first version of that generalisation was a real weakening."},{"id":"spn-74813","text":" It asserted only \"one canonical, all stale annotated\" — under which "},{"id":"spn-74814","marks":["bold"],"text":"deleting `@1` outright passes"},{"id":"spn-74815","text":". The forgery for it kept being caught, but by a "},{"id":"spn-74816","marks":["italic"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-74817","text":" assertion that happens to require "},{"id":"spn-74818","marks":["code"],"text":"@1"},{"id":"spn-74819","text":" to exist. That is the coincidental-second-occurrence species for the "},{"id":"spn-74820","marks":["bold"],"text":"fourth"},{"id":"spn-74821","text":" time in this line. Fixed by requiring revisions to run 1..N contiguously, so a withdrawn round cannot hide behind a survivor."}]},{"id":"blk-41896","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74822","text":"Where the measurement now stands"}]},{"id":"blk-41897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74823","marks":["code"],"text":"measure_compare.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74824","text":" (non-gating, "},{"id":"spn-74825","marks":["code"],"text":"make gov-measure"},{"id":"spn-74826","text":"): "},{"id":"spn-74827","marks":["bold"],"text":"35/35"},{"id":"spn-74828","text":" — the 24-vector corpus, three film fixtures, the three ERA fixtures, and five single-dup-head fixtures. Still no expected table in the emitter or the comparator; "},{"id":"spn-74829","marks":["code"],"text":"grid_check"},{"id":"spn-74830","text":" refuses the fixture term in either."}]},{"id":"blk-41898","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74831","text":"Next, in your order"}]},{"id":"blk-41899","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74832","marks":["bold"],"text":"BUDGET_EXHAUSTED as native film evidence"},{"id":"spn-74833","text":" rather than the typed refusal it is now."}]}],"id":"blk-41900","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74834","marks":["bold"],"text":"`EMISSION_CONFORMANCE-v1`"},{"id":"spn-74835","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-74836","marks":["code"],"text":"{closed_template → target_term_sem_id}"},{"id":"spn-74837","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-41902","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74838","text":"Also unclaimed and unchanged: C-side replay (films flow C→JS only); alias "},{"id":"spn-74839","marks":["bold"],"text":"precedence"},{"id":"spn-74840","text":" if a well-formed fixture ever produces one; and a direct negative fixture for "},{"id":"spn-74841","marks":["code"],"text":"film-projection-not-unique"},{"id":"spn-74842","text":" if the representation can express two reachable matching projections safely — you said not to pull that ahead, and I have not."}]},{"id":"blk-41905","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-74843","text":"Files"}]},{"id":"blk-41906","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74844","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_B4_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-74845","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-74846","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-74847","text":" replays every gate "},{"id":"spn-74848","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-74849","text":" the non-gating measurement"}]}],"id":"blk-41907","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74850","text":"from any extraction dir, writing "},{"id":"spn-74851","marks":["code"],"text":"RESULTS.txt"},{"id":"spn-74852","text":" from the run."}]},{"id":"blk-41910","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74853","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/round-11-ledger.md"},{"id":"spn-74854","text":" § B4 (items 299–308)."}]}],"id":"blk-41911","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74855","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/bridge/ic32_film.c"},{"id":"spn-74856","text":" v0.4.0 · "},{"id":"spn-74857","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/film_check.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74858","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-74859","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge/measure_compare.mjs"},{"id":"spn-74860","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-41913","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-74861","text":"Reproduce: "},{"id":"spn-74862","marks":["code"],"text":"make gov-measure"},{"id":"spn-74863","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-74864","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32_film --probe-whnf \"<term>\""},{"id":"spn-74865","text":" for the neutrality witness."}]}],"id":"blk-41915","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraiyavwzgyuxvoh6c2wrn3tdl727nj3zrqtvsa5qhhfbvt6mf6fora","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}